on the trunk. A compact rosette of about 25–30 short fronds, with the lower fronds pointing below the crown base. A light-green spear shows at the apex.", "render-1 (seed 42): one unbranched trunk leaning steadily to the right. The curve tightens in the top quarter, just below the crown. The bend goes one way only and does not reverse, so it reads as a gentle lean with one curve, not a wave. Diameter is near-constant apart from the basal flare. The crown matches seed 1: short fronds with lower ones drooping.", "render-2 (P-TRUNK, seed 1): at close range the fronds show more droop and some recurve. Leaflets are small, leaf-like and loosely spaced along each rachis. The trunk is smooth with a sparse spiral of small conical stubs.", "render-3 (P-BASE, seed 1; metadata visibility 'hidden'): a close, heavily shadowed view of smooth trunk surface with four isolated cup- or wedge-shaped stubs. The drawn surface is readable enough to judge stub density.", "Finish: clean shading, silhouette and ground shadow are at or above the finish floor of the spruce anchor (anchor-0). The anchor was used for finish only, not for morphology.", "reference-0 shows an S-curved, leaning trunk with a swollen base. reference-1 and reference-2 show a straight trunk. The owner's straight or gently leaning requirement is within this range.", "Leaf-base stubs are retained trunk tissue, not growth on the trunk, so their presence does not break the owner's bare-trunk priority. Ferns on the trunk in reference-1 and reference-2 are variation, and the owner has excluded them."], "findings": [{"observation": "Fronds are short compared with tree height. The crown spread is roughly half that of reference-0 in proportion, and the fronds do not read as long arching feather leaves.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Frond length and leaflet-size dials are too low; the owner names these as the first dials."}, {"observation": "Leaflets are small, sparse and jagged, so each frond looks thin. The references show long, narrow, stiff leaflets in a dense plume.", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "The lowest fronds droop below the crown base in both seeds. The rosette arrangement from a single apex is present.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "The seed 1 trunk is straight and vertical. The seed 42 trunk leans and curves one way near the top without reversing. Both have near-constant diameter apart from a basal flare.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "The seed 42 trunk curves more tightly in the upper quarter than lower down. It is not wavy, but it is a visible bend rather than a uniform lean.", "evidence_ids": ["render-1"], "impact": "variation", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Nothing grows on either trunk: no fronds, branches or epiphytes. There are only small leaf-base stubs.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "The trunk surface is smooth with sparse isolated stubs. There is no dense spiral diamond lattice and no fibre.", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "The fn-110 trunk organs are landed, but stub density and size are far below the reference, and no fibre fill is drawn."}, {"observation": "The P-BASE render is marked visibility 'hidden' in its metadata, but the drawn trunk surface and stubs can still be read.", "evidence_ids": ["render-3"], "impact": "variation", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "No fruit bunches appear in any render. Fruit is seen only in reference-0. The reference-1 crown base shows no bunches, which suggests fruit is not always present.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "required_unknown", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": "The fn-111 date cluster has not landed."}, {"observation": "Finish quality meets the anchor's finish floor.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "anchor-0"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}], "coverage": [{"trait_id": "crown-pinnate-arching-fronds", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "The rosette from one apex and the drooping lower fronds are present. However, the fronds are short and mostly straight, with a crown about half the reference's size relative to the tree. The inventory calls for long, progressively recurved fronds, so this is a defining mismatch."}, {"trait_id": "leaflet-arrangement-stiff-narrow", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-0", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Leaflets are small, sparse, jagged blades in a thin row along each rachis. They are not long, narrow, stiff leaflets set in groups at different angles to form a plume."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-leaf-base-diamond-pattern", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Only what is drawn was judged. The drawn trunk has sparse isolated conical or cup-shaped stubs on a smooth surface, not a tessellated spiral lattice of blunt wedges."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-fibrous-matting", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "No fibre is drawn between stubs; the surface is smooth and uniform."}, {"trait_id": "